Third-party software dependencies
---------------------------------

Flow Read is built with Flutter and Dart and uses third-party packages listed
in pubspec.yaml and pubspec.lock. Those dependencies remain under their own
licenses. Review the package metadata from pub.dev and the generated Flutter
license registry before redistributing a release build.

Bundled lexical data
--------------------

The files under assets/wordnet/ are generated from an English WordNet 2025 JSON
source. Open English WordNet is published by the Global WordNet Association and
is released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0):

https://github.com/globalwordnet/english-wordnet

Open English WordNet incorporates and extends WordNet material. Preserve the
upstream attribution and any WordNet copyright/license terms required by the
exact source archive used for the bundled generated files:

https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use

The source archive is not committed to this repository. Before a stable
release, verify the exact upstream archive and keep the required upstream
license and attribution with the release artifacts.

The files under assets/dict/ contain an English word-form mapping used by the
local reader and vocabulary features. Before a stable release, verify the
source and redistribution terms for the exact dictionary source used to build
this asset.

Project media
-------------

The files under assets/brand/ and the app screenshots used in README.md are
project assets unless a separate source is documented. Do not add third-party
images to these directories without recording their license and attribution in
this file.

Online dictionary sources
-------------------------

Flow Read can request dictionary content from external online services or
websites such as dictionaryapi.dev, Collins, and Longman when those sources are
enabled. These services and websites are not bundled with Flow Read and are
subject to their own terms. Online sources must remain optional and must keep a
local/offline fallback available for the reader.
